

### 384 BESSEL FUNCTIONS OF INTEGER ORDER

For _n_=0 these expressions give the _s_th zero of each function; for other values of \(n\) the zeros represented may not be the _s_th.

**Uniform Asymptotic Expansions for Large Orders**

When \(n\) is large and positive

**9.10.37**

\[{\rm ber},(\nu z)+i~{}{\rm bei},(\nu z)\sim\]

\[\frac{e^{\pi i}}{\sqrt{2\pi k}}\left(\frac{xe^{\pi i/i}}{1+\xi}\right)^{\ast} \langle 1+\sum\limits_{k=1}^{m}\frac{u_{k}(\xi^{-1})}{\nu^{k}}\rangle\]

**9.10.38**

\[{\rm ker},(\nu z)+i~{}{\rm kei},(\nu x)\]

\[\sim\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2\nu\xi}}~{}e^{-it}\Big{(}\frac{ze^{\pi i/i}}{1+\xi} \Big{)}^{-\nu}\langle 1+\sum\limits_{k=1}^{m}(-)^{k}\frac{u_{k}(\xi^{-1})}{\nu^{k}}\rangle\]

**9.10.39**

\[{\rm ber}^{\prime}_{\prime}(\nu x)+i~{}{\rm bei}^{\prime}_{\prime}(\nu z)\]

\[\sim\sqrt{\frac{\xi}{2\pi r}}~{}\frac{e^{\pi i}}{x}\Big{(}\frac{ze^{\pi i/i}}{1 +\xi}\Big{)}^{-\nu}\langle 1+\sum\limits_{k=1}^{m}\frac{v_{k}(\xi^{-1})}{\nu^{k}}\rangle\]

**9.10.40**

\[{\rm ker}^{\prime}_{\prime}(\nu x)+i~{}{\rm kei}^{\prime}_{\prime}(\nu x)\]

\[\sim\!-\sqrt{\frac{\pi\xi}{2\nu}}~{}\frac{e^{-it}}{x}\Big{(}\frac{ze^{\pi i/i} }{1+\xi}\Big{)}^{-\nu}\langle 1+\sum\limits_{k=1}^{m}(-)^{k}\frac{v_{k}(\xi^{-1})}{\nu^{k}}\rangle\]

where

**9.10.41**

\[\xi\!=\!\sqrt{1+ix^{3}}\]

and \(u_{k}(t),t_{k}(t)\) are given by **9.3.9** and **9.3.13.** All fractional powers take their principal values.

